# KaliWebApp Environment Configuration

Create these files in the root of the KaliWebApp frontend directory for environment-specific configurations.

## Development Configuration (.env.development.local)

```env
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
```

## Production Configuration (.env.production.local)

```env
VITE_API_URL=https://your-production-api.com/api
```

## Testing Configuration (.env.test.local)

```env
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api
```

## How to Use

1. Create a `.env.development.local` file in the frontend root
2. Add your development API URL
3. Vite will automatically load this file in development mode
4. Access via `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`

## Example in Code

```javascript
const API_URL = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL || 'http://localhost:5000/api';

fetch(`${API_URL}/auth/login`, {
  method: 'POST',
  body: JSON.stringify(credentials)
})
```

## Important Notes

- Files named `.env.*.local` are NOT tracked by git (they're in .gitignore)
- Environment variables must be prefixed with `VITE_` to be exposed to the frontend
- Use `.env.example` as a template for team members
- Never commit actual environment files

## Available Files

- `.env` - Loaded in all cases (commit this with defaults)
- `.env.local` - Loaded in all cases (don't commit)
- `.env.development` - Only loaded in dev (commit this with defaults)
- `.env.development.local` - Only loaded in dev (don't commit)
- `.env.production` - Only loaded in build/preview (commit this with defaults)
- `.env.production.local` - Only loaded in build/preview (don't commit)
